<title>LEBANON: Lebanon PM heads for Washington donors' conference.</title>
<headline>Lebanon PM heads for Washington donors' conference.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanese Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri flew to Paris on Friday en route to Washington where he will attend a U.S.-sponsored &quot;Friends of Lebanon&quot; donors' conference on Monday.</p>
<p>Lebanon wants donor governments at the one-day conference to pledge $5 billion over five years for 31 infrastructure projects which the government cannot afford but considers high priority for its post-civil war reconstruction drive.</p>
</text>
